RSX/MSL: the translation cache names its translator by a hash of its sources, not its build time.

Upstream's MSL translation cache (#511, PS3RECOMP_MSL_CACHE=<dir>, host/main.cpp sets ./cache/msl) marks each file
with the translator that wrote it, and takes the build time for that. build_host.sh rebuilds the toolkit from a clean
tree whenever a patch changes, so every such rebuild retired the whole cache, and the first run after it stalled the
FIFO walker on every shader again (Resistance 3's opening cutscene: walker passes of 160-360 ms, the woman's head
jerking back and forth). CMake now passes a hash of rsx_shader_msl.cpp/.h (PS3RECOMP_MSL_TRANSLATOR_ID; both files
are configure dependencies); without it the build time stays.

Test: two builds configured apart from the same sources (scripts/build_host.sh and the toolkit test build) define
the same PS3RECOMP_MSL_TRANSLATOR_ID; with the build time they never did.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index edc8545c..0db1a8ea 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -279,2 +279,17 @@ if(UNIX)
         endif()
+        # The translator's identity in the MSL translation cache: a hash of its
+        # sources, so a rebuild that changes nothing keeps the cached files and
+        # an edit to the translator retires them. (Its build time did the
+        # latter too, and threw the whole cache away on every rebuild.)
+        set(_msl_sources libs/video/rsx_shader_msl.cpp libs/video/rsx_shader_msl.h)
+        set(_msl_text "")
+        foreach(f IN LISTS _msl_sources)
+            file(SHA256 "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/${f}" _h)
+            string(APPEND _msl_text "${_h}")
+        endforeach()
+        string(SHA256 _msl_id "${_msl_text}")
+        string(SUBSTRING "${_msl_id}" 0 23 _msl_id)
+        set_property(DIRECTORY APPEND PROPERTY CMAKE_CONFIGURE_DEPENDS ${_msl_sources})
+        target_compile_definitions(ps3recomp_msl_translation INTERFACE
+            "PS3RECOMP_MSL_TRANSLATOR_ID=\"${_msl_id}\"")
         target_link_libraries(ps3recomp_runtime PRIVATE ps3recomp_msl_translation)
diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_shader_msl.cpp b/libs/video/rsx_shader_msl.cpp
index 7dc6fd7f..473470fa 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_shader_msl.cpp
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_shader_msl.cpp
@@ -226,3 +226,12 @@ const u32 kCacheFormat = 1;
 const u32 kCacheMagic = 0x4C534D52u;   /* "RMSL" */
+/* The translator's identity: what it was built from stands for the front-end
+ * and spirv-cross options above and the binding contract in rsx_shader_msl.h.
+ * The build passes a hash of those two files (CMakeLists.txt), so the files an
+ * older translator wrote become misses and a plain rebuild keeps them; without
+ * it, this file's compile time stands in, which retires them on every rebuild. */
+#ifdef PS3RECOMP_MSL_TRANSLATOR_ID
+const char kTranslatorBuild[24] = PS3RECOMP_MSL_TRANSLATOR_ID;
+#else
 const char kTranslatorBuild[24] = __DATE__ " " __TIME__;
+#endif
 
